{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["תקח לה — what is in her hand. For I will not send to her anymore." "פן נהיה לבוז — to go after the consecrated woman, i.e., to pursue her further."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The lemma quotes Judah's words to his friend Hirah; Rashbam explains Judah means she may keep whatever pledge-object she already holds.", 1 "Rashbam reads לבוז as 'to pursue/desire' connected to the root בזז in the sense of seeking booty, or alternatively reads the phrase as 'lest we become objects of contempt by pursuing her.' The translation preserves the ambiguity."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:39.108768181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}